21: /// <remarks>
22: /// <para><b>Frame convention</b> — for each role the frame quaternion <c>F</c> rotates unit
23: /// axes onto: <c>X = P</c> (primary), <c>Z</c> = the secondary hint <c>S</c> orthonormalized
24: /// against <c>P</c>, <c>Y = cross(Z, X)</c> (right-handed; for fingers Y is the curl hinge).</para>
25: /// <para><b>Primary axis P</b> = normalize(chain-child head − bone head), where the chain
26: /// child is the next <i>mapped</i> role down the bone's anatomical chain
27: /// (Hips→Spine0..4→Neck→Head; Clavicle→UpperArm→LowerArm→Hand; UpperLeg→LowerLeg→Foot→Toe;
28: /// per-finger Meta→Prox→Mid→Dist). Tips: the Head inherits its previous chain segment
29: /// (neck→head — the skull-base axis, real anatomy; measured 0–27° forward of character up
30: /// across neutral-rest rigs), falling back to a virtual character-up extension only when
31: /// that segment is absent or degenerate; Hand points at the midpoint of its mapped finger
32: /// proximals (else along the forearm); Foot without a toe and Toe extend along character
33: /// forward; finger distals extend along their previous segment. Other bones with nothing
34: /// mapped below inherit the previous chain segment's direction. A single mapped finger
35: /// joint uses its direct child/end-site as its real segment direction when available.</para>
36: /// <para><b>Secondary axis S</b> by bone class: spine/neck/head/hips and legs use character
37: /// forward (knee hinge lateral); clavicle/arms/hands use <c>cross(P, characterUp)</c>
38: /// (elbow hinge ⊥ limb in the character's horizontal plane at T-pose), falling back to
39: /// character forward when P is vertical; feet/toes use character up; fingers use the hand's
40: /// dorsal palm normal (see <see cref="HandGeometry.Dorsal"/>) so a positive rotation about
41: /// frame Y curls fingertips toward the palm on both hands.</para>
42: /// <para>When used by the solver, build the frames on the <see cref="RestNormalizer"/>-
43: /// normalized rest via <see cref="Build(SkeletonModel, MappingResult, IReadOnlyList{XForm})"/>;
44: /// this class itself just measures whatever rest it is given.</para>
45: /// </remarks>
